- `defines(v1, ...)`: Range only contains `{"Delivery crew picks up items at event site"}`, omitting the source alternative `"Customer returns the items to the store"`.
- `defines(v3, ...)` and `defines(v6, ...)`: Ranges only contain `{"Stored for future orders"}`, omitting the source alternative `"Items are packed for an existing order"` for both disposition steps.
- `defines(v4, ...)`: Range only contains `{"Customer does not return missing items"}`, omitting the source alternative `"Customer returns the missing items"`.
- `guard(b3, n15, ...)` and `guard(b6, n16, ...)`: Only guard the storing option; omit guards and outgoing edges for `"Items are packed for an existing order"`, incorrectly collapsing a documented choice into a single path.
- `guard(b4, n8, ...)`: Only guards the negative response; omits the guard and outgoing edge for `"Customer returns the missing items"`.
- `precedence(b4, n8)` terminating at `end(e1)`: Source explicitly states both missing-item responses `"continue the process"`, but the model ends execution prematurely instead of proceeding to subsequent steps.
- `precedence(n13, c1)` and `converge(c1)`: Source implies discarded items conclude their subflow after `"email the customer with replacement charges"`, but the model forces this path to merge via `c1` and continue to `n14` ("Items disposition after repair"), distorting the chronological flow.
- `b1`, `b3`, `b4`, `b6`: Declared as XOR branches but only define one guarded outgoing edge each; missing complementary guards/edges violate the mutually exclusive choice semantics required by the source text.

Structural Check
- [S1] STC9 failed: Each branch node must have exactly one incoming and at least two outgoing edges. | Node `b1` has in=1 and out=1. | Node `b3` has in=1 and out=1. | Node `b4` has in=1 and out=1. | Node `b6` has in=1 and out=1. | DSL: branch(b1,XOR); branch(b3,XOR); branch(b4,XOR); branch(b6,XOR)
- [S2] STC11 failed: Each variable definition must have a valid range with at least two distinct values. | Variable `v1` has an invalid range `['Delivery crew picks up items at event site']`. | Variable `v3` has an invalid range `['Stored for future orders']`. | Variable `v4` has an invalid range `['Customer does not return missing items']`. | Variable `v6` has an invalid range `['Stored for future orders']`.
- [S3] STC15 failed: Every variable used in a guard must be formally defined. | Guard `v1 = 'Delivery crew picks up items at event site'` on `b1 -> n3` uses undefined variable `v1`. | Guard `v4 = 'Customer does not return missing items'` on `b4 -> n8` uses undefined variable `v4`. | Guard `v3 = 'Stored for future orders'` on `b3 -> n15` uses undefined variable `v3`. | Guard `v6 = 'Stored for future orders'` on `b6 -> n16` uses undefined variable `v6`. | DSL: guard(b1,n3,"v1 = 'Delivery crew picks up items at event site'"); guard(b4,n8,"v4 = 'Customer does not return missing items'"); guard(b3,n15,"v3 = 'Stored for future orders'"); guard(b6,n16,"v6 = 'Stored for future orders'")

Logical Sanity Check
- [L1] LSC1 failed: Every guard must be satisfiable under the declared ranges of its referenced variables. | Guard `v1 = 'Delivery crew picks up items at event site'` on `b1 -> n3` cannot be evaluated: `v1` has no declared range. | Guard `v4 = 'Customer does not return missing items'` on `b4 -> n8` cannot be evaluated: `v4` has no declared range. | Guard `v3 = 'Stored for future orders'` on `b3 -> n15` cannot be evaluated: `v3` has no declared range. | Guard `v6 = 'Stored for future orders'` on `b6 -> n16` cannot be evaluated: `v6` has no declared range. | DSL: guard(b1,n3,"v1 = 'Delivery crew picks up items at event site'"); guard(b4,n8,"v4 = 'Customer does not return missing items'"); guard(b3,n15,"v3 = 'Stored for future orders'"); guard(b6,n16,"v6 = 'Stored for future orders'")
- [L2] LSC3 failed: Guards outgoing from XOR/OR branches must cover the whole evaluated state space. | Branch `b1` cannot be evaluated: `v1` has no declared range. | Branch `b3` cannot be evaluated: `v3` has no declared range. | Branch `b4` cannot be evaluated: `v4` has no declared range. | Branch `b6` cannot be evaluated: `v6` has no declared range.
